"view.progressivecalendar.help"                          = "Select the techniques and factors to scan, choose which event kinds to include, set the orbs, and enter a start and end date. Then click 'Calculate' to search the Progressive Calendar for events.\n\nDates must be in the format yyyy/mm/dd, using the standard Gregorian calendar. The end date must be after the start date.\n\nScanning is more expensive for fast-moving factors (like a transiting Moon) over a long period, so the maximum allowed span shrinks as fast factors are added to the selection. The current limit is shown below the date fields.\n\nTransits and secondary directions can produce aspects, parallels, cusp conjunctions, retrograde/direct stations, out-of-bounds transitions and declination extremes. Symbolic directions only produce longitude-based results: aspects to radix, aspects between symbolic factors, and cusp conjunctions.\n\nEnigma uses your configuration settings by default, but you can change them here for a single calculation; use 'Reset to configuration' to revert.";
