"view.progressivecalendar.results.title"                 = "Progressive Calendar";
"view.progressivecalendar.results.noresults"             = "Enter a date range and press Calculate to see progressive events.";
"view.progressivecalendar.results.help"                  = "The diagram shows, for each technique, the aspects and parallels as shapes that grow from zero at orb-entry to a peak at the exact moment and shrink back to zero at orb-exit. Out-of-bounds moments are shown alongside them as ticks. Below that, retrograde/direct stations, cusp conjunctions and declination extremes are grouped one row per factor. Click anywhere in the diagram to see the exact date and time at that point.\n\nThe 'Aspects & Parallels' table lists every episode with the date it entered orb, became exact, and left orb again (a dash means the episode was already in orb at the start, or is still in orb at the end, of the scanned period). The 'Other events' table lists the remaining, instantaneous events with their date and ecliptical position.";
